AG CuteMusic on Windows
=======================

Built on GitHub's Windows runner (.github/workflows/windows.yml) from the AG Projects darcs repository synced to
GitHub: Python, PyQt6 and GStreamer (the GStreamer project's own Python wheels, 1.28+:
gstreamer-bundle) packed into one folder by PyInstaller, a zip of it and an installer (Inno Setup, per user, no
admin rights).

The workflow lives in .github/workflows, recorded in darcs so the sync carries it: record and push as usual. A
build runs only when the version changes (__version__ in cutemusic/__init__.py), on a tag, or by hand (Actions ->
Windows -> Run workflow), not on every patch. The build is in the GitHub repository's Actions tab: its artifact
AG-CuteMusic-windows holds AG-CuteMusic-<version>-setup.exe and AG-CuteMusic-<version>-windows.zip.
Each build is tried too: the self test plays a test song to its end through the app's Player (into a fakesink),
then the Trial step installs the setup.exe silently, starts the app, takes a screenshot after 20 s and uninstalls it;
the screenshot and the app's logs are the artifact AG-CuteMusic-windows-trial. A tag (a darcs
tag the sync turns into a git one) also makes a GitHub release with them.

On a Windows machine (Python 3.10+ 64-bit from python.org, Inno Setup 6 for the installer):

  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File windows\make-standalone.ps1

The files:

  make-standalone.ps1   the build: venv, PyInstaller, GStreamer next to the executable, self test, zip, installer
  ag-cute-music.spec    PyInstaller's: the app folder, without GStreamer (copied in as it is)
  standalone.py         the executable's script: GStreamer's environment set up before gi is imported;
                        AG_CUTEMUSIC_SELFTEST=<file>: GStreamer, its elements and every module checked, then exit
  installer.iss         Inno Setup's
  make_ico.py           icons/ag-cute-music.svg into the .ico
  requirements.txt      what the build venv gets

Not on Windows: the mixer as a sound device for Blink (the AG Podcast Mixer link, link.py: a driver on macOS,
PipeWire nodes on Linux); the media keys work while the window has the focus (no MPRIS, no Now Playing). Settings and
logs are in %USERPROFILE%\.ag-cute-music.
